    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T23:46:16Z",
    "body": "Local commit ed725f5 on issue/54-dflat-wrap (not pushed yet).\n\nRoot cause: the wrap closed the developed sheet's two free ends with a meridian wall in the plane of the cover's extreme column (s_lo / s_hi). On a revolve the seam column is straight and lies in that plane. On a D-flat across the ±π branch, the flat's vertices sit at their own azimuths, so the seam column is ragged and the wall met none of its edges, which left dangling chord ends.\n\nFix: `multiaxis::rotary_seam`. An edge whose two facets develop it one period apart is a seam edge. Its first-copy version and its second-copy version each hang a vertical curtain down to the floor radius. On a revolve this is the old wall, split on the same diagonal, so the OffsetRings digest is unchanged. The wrap also now refuses an open mesh by name up front. On main, a hole that no level slices through wrapped silently.\n\nPinned by `rotary_dflat::{a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement, a_bar_with_a_hole_in_its_skin_is_still_refused_by_name, a_flat_channel_across_the_seam_is_refused_adaptive_by_name_and_rings_cut_it}`. All three fail on main. The last one is #9's seam law end to end; it lives in the new suite because `rotary_adaptive.rs` is at the 400-line budget.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
